# Shared pagination

Every list that can grow uses one pager and one page contract. Do not add a second pager, a "load more" control, or a local `limit` on a new screen.

## Client

Import `Pagination` and `PAGE_SIZE` from `@/shared/ui`. Pass `page`, `pageSize`, `total`, and `onPageChange`. Hide the pager when `total` is 0.

```jsx
// ❌ BAD — a private pager or a fixed slice
const rows = data.slice(0, 50);
<button type="button" onClick={() => setPage(page + 1)}>Next</button>

// ✅ GOOD
import { PAGE_SIZE, Pagination } from '@/shared/ui/index.js';

<Pagination
  page={page}
  pageSize={PAGE_SIZE}
  total={total}
  disabled={query.isFetching}
  onPageChange={setPage}
/>
```

Reset `page` to 1 when the filters change. A dropdown that chooses from a long list uses the same component under the control.

## Server

Build the query with `pageQueryShape`, `pageSlice`, and `pageBody` from `server/src/shared/pagination.js`. The success body stays `{ success: true, data }`, and `data` is `{ items, page, pageSize, total }`.

- Default page size is 20. The maximum is 100.
- `page` starts at 1. `page` below 1 or `pageSize` outside 1–100 is `400` `VALIDATION_ERROR`.
- Count the full filter, then `skip` / `take` that page. Do not page a query that another workflow needs in full, such as discovery of every care context.
- Document `page` and `pageSize` on the OpenAPI path in the same change.
